Remote model list: every provider the dashboard calls configured.

Hermes One (v0.7.8) lists a remote dashboard's models from
GET /api/model/options, but keeps only the current provider's row and
user-defined endpoints (shouldIncludeRemoteOptionProvider). A built-in
provider configured with a key, OpenRouter via OPENROUTER_API_KEY on
dave-hermes (`source: built-in`, `is_current: false`), was therefore
dropped whole: no OpenRouter model at all while anthropic is current.

The app now asks for `?explicit_only=true` (hermes' own filter for
desktop pickers: only explicitly configured providers, no ambient or
auto-seeded credentials) and lists every row it returns except the MoA
pseudo-provider. Tests: tests/remote-models.test.ts (new case with
dave-hermes' row shapes; the configured-only case's fake dashboard
honours the flag; the named-profile case now expects its second
provider) and the IPC test's request path.

